  "summary": "Software Developer, Senior Staff\n\nQualcomm Inc. / San Diego / 2021 – current\nADAS Automotive R&D research and implementation of future capabilities for Mobile World Conference in Barcelona\n\n•\tDesigned and Implemented cloud service that integrated with additional cloud infrastructure for vehicle and pedestrian safety applications.\n•\tMultithreaded application design where scalability and latency were of interest.\n•\tIntegration of software from multiple teams often times in research phases for demonstrations\n•\tLed new research projects, mentored team members on development of research concepts for demo applications.\n\nQualcomm Inc. / San Diego / 2015 – 2021\nPrimary role focused on Android Kernel development where I was responsible for feature design and implementation in accordance to US government customer requirements.\n\n•\tAndroid kernel feature development for security features for government partners\n•\tAuthored and designed custom internally used Arm toolchain to address code size and functionality requirements\n•\tKernel debugging using crash logs, kernel source, disassembly\n•\tBuild systems with GNU Make and Scons\n•\tPython test framework design and planning including the python to C application interface complete with requirements mapping for tracking.\n•\tOther exposure areas: elf format and manipulation, Android OS, AES encryption, ARM assembly, Networking\n\nSoftware Test Developer\nQualcomm Inc. / San Diego / 2003 - 2014\n\nWorked across teams to gather and plan for new product requirements and features. Led the tasking and planning for automation framework within the team.\n•\tLead a team of engineers to develop and deliver testability capabilities and enhancements.\n•\tDesigned and developed new systems to manage testing activity",
